  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to the Open Government Partnership</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The UK is a founding member of the Open Government Partnership (OGP) and served as co-chair until September 2013. This is now a movement that includes 61 governments, each of whom have met eligibility criteria and made significant commitments to open government. The OGP has the potential to advance recent progress in transparency and open government through peer learning, research and evidence gathering. To support the work of this growing movement the secretariat is in particular need of core support to ensure impact, sustainability and value for money from this initiative.</narrative>
  </description>
